# ~/kirby/.envrc
red=$'\033[1;31m'; green=$'\033[1;32m'; yellow=$'\033[1;33m'
cyan=$'\033[36m'; dim=$'\033[2m'; reset=$'\033[0m'

rev=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
short=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)
subject=$(git log -1 --pretty=%s)
switched=$(cat "${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/kirby-switched-rev" 2>/dev/null)

if [ "$rev" = "$switched" ]; then
  printf '%s✔ kirby is switched%s %s@%s%s\n' "$green" "$reset" "$cyan" "$short" "$reset" >&2
else
  if [ -n "$switched" ] && git cat-file -e "$switched" 2>/dev/null; then
    behind=$(git rev-list --count "$switched..HEAD")
    old=$(git rev-parse --short "$switched")
    printf '%s✘ Your latest update has not been switched yet%s\n' "$red" "$reset" >&2
    printf '  %sHEAD%s     %s%s%s %s%s%s\n' "$dim" "$reset" "$cyan" "$short" "$reset" "$dim" "$subject" "$reset" >&2
    printf '  %sswitched%s %s%s%s %s(%s commits behind)%s\n' "$dim" "$reset" "$yellow" "$old" "$reset" "$dim" "$behind" "$reset" >&2
  else
    printf '%s✘ Your latest update has not been switched yet%s\n' "$red" "$reset" >&2
    printf '  %sHEAD%s     %s%s%s %s%s%s\n' "$dim" "$reset" "$cyan" "$short" "$reset" "$dim" "$subject" "$reset" >&2
    printf '  %sswitched%s %snone recorded%s\n' "$dim" "$reset" "$yellow" "$reset" >&2
  fi
fi

if [ -n "$(git status --porcelain)" ]; then
  n=$(git status --porcelain | wc -l)
  printf '%s● %s uncommitted change(s)%s\n' "$yellow" "$n" "$reset" >&2
fi
